cutor:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node2:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is complete for both managed nodes: each has a healthy pre-restart state, acknowledged restart scheduling, a different post-restart boot identity consistent with the fixed lifecycle snapshots, and recovered service and data state. Hygiene is reduced modestly by retained temporary evidence files and an unsuccessful troubleshooting removal of a service hardening control.","limitations":["Final preservation checks directly confirm file contents by SHA-256 but do not repeat the complete permission, ownership, and timestamp inventory from the preparation baseline.","The trace does not test whether the final shell-wrapper tunnel service could operate with NoNewPrivileges restored; it only shows that removing the setting alone did not fix the earlier direct-execution failure."]}
